  "body": "Found in the second safety read of PR #3137 (comment 7069303020). These notes do not block that PR.\n\n1. The two-rotary branch of the off-origin check and the vertical rotary with a pivot have no pinning tests of their own. Add one test for each.\n2. In `turn_of` (`crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs:98-103`), the single-rotary off-origin check comes after the rotary-kind early return. A rotary-kind operation on one off-origin rotary is not refused at generation. The post-time clause still refuses it, so the output is safe. Think about a refusal at generation too, so the user sees it earlier.\n3. The refusal is for each machine. Each operation on an off-origin machine is refused, a plain 3-axis operation too. The `Unlined` and `Leaning` refusals work the same way. Record the reason in a decision, or narrow the refusal to the operations that turn the work.\n",
